{"jobs":[{"id":"f54b61ac-5744-40fc-93d0-fd74e67de4b5","title":"Product Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"GMT / BST (UK, Portugal, Ireland)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-07-04T15:57:29.293+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/f54b61ac-5744-40fc-93d0-fd74e67de4b5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/f54b61ac-5744-40fc-93d0-fd74e67de4b5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Short on time? </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> You’re an experienced product builder. You’re motivated to help predict chronic diseases - faster and more affordably</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> Team size 45, 7 engineers, revenue 4x'd in the last year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> £90K - £130K + equity </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Fully remote (GMT timezone)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why we need you</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our small (for now) but mighty 6-person engineering team is tackling big, ambitious problems across wearables and lab testing. We’re already:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Streaming time-series data from 3M+ wearables every second</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Helping major digital health companies deliver 4M+ lab tests across all 50 US states</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Saving millions of patients thousands of dollars</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Now we’re aiming even higher: going from 4 million lab tests to 40 million diagnostics in the next year. To get there, we need full-stack engineers who can help us build the next version of our diagnostics API.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You don’t need healthcare experience but you do need to:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get excited about shipping features that can cut medical bills by 10x</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be curious enough to unpack messy insurance incentives and parse thousands of records to estimate true out-of-pocket costs for patients</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ask sharp questions to take a problem from “rough idea” to shipped software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay pragmatic and comfortable navigating domain experts, constraints, and real-world edge cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Care deeply about UX: build interfaces that feel intuitive and clearly communicate complex healthcare information</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Building our customer facing products:</strong> we have dashboards for both product verticals, wearables and lab testing. For example, the lab testing dashboard allows customers to self serve and order lab tests for their patients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Speaking with customers:</strong> for this role, we need you to be customer obsessed, asking thought-provoking questions and digging into product usage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Owning features across the stack:</strong> You'll own features end-to-end across frontend and backend, and in the cloud. You'll build new functionality, design clean APIs, and manage reliable, fault-tolerant services and pipelines in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tackling ambitious problems:</strong> you’ll be breaking down technical challenges that haven’t been done before in healthcare, we need you to be extremely product minded with every line of code you write</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Iterating quickly:</strong> ship, learn from real usage, and refine to make the experience better each time.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup engineering experience where you influenced what to build, not just how to build it</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: you’ve built something from 0 → 1</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of building and shipping full-stack features end-to-end</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to turn messy or unclear problems into a clear plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working across frontend and backend (perfection in both not required)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong product judgment - within a clear product direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Focus on how people actually use the product, not just code elegance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fast iteration based on feedback and metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working in a domain with hard constraints and complex real-world edge cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactive about getting feedback from customers on what you ship</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>You don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How you'll be compensated</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary: £90K - £130K + equity </p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\nShort on time? \n\n - You: You’re an experienced product builder. You’re motivated to help predict chronic diseases - faster and more affordably\n\n - Us: Team size 45, 7 engineers, revenue 4x'd in the last year\n\n - Salary: £90K - £130K + equity \n\n - Location: Fully remote (GMT timezone)\n   \n   \n\nWhy we need you\n\nOur small (for now) but mighty 6-person engineering team is tackling big, ambitious problems across wearables and lab testing. We’re already:\n\n - Streaming time-series data from 3M+ wearables every second\n\n - Helping major digital health companies deliver 4M+ lab tests across all 50 US states\n\n - Saving millions of patients thousands of dollars\n\nNow we’re aiming even higher: going from 4 million lab tests to 40 million diagnostics in the next year. To get there, we need full-stack engineers who can help us build the next version of our diagnostics API.\n\nYou don’t need healthcare experience but you do need to:\n\n - Get excited about shipping features that can cut medical bills by 10x\n\n - Be curious enough to unpack messy insurance incentives and parse thousands of records to estimate true out-of-pocket costs for patients\n\n - Ask sharp questions to take a problem from “rough idea” to shipped software\n\n - Stay pragmatic and comfortable navigating domain experts, constraints, and real-world edge cases\n\n - Care deeply about UX: build interfaces that feel intuitive and clearly communicate complex healthcare information\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll be doing day to day\n\n - Building our customer facing products: we have dashboards for both product verticals, wearables and lab testing. For example, the lab testing dashboard allows customers to self serve and order lab tests for their patients.\n\n - Speaking with customers: for this role, we need you to be customer obsessed, asking thought-provoking questions and digging into product usage\n\n - Owning features across the stack: You'll own features end-to-end across frontend and backend, and in the cloud. You'll build new functionality, design clean APIs, and manage reliable, fault-tolerant services and pipelines in production.\n\n - Tackling ambitious problems: you’ll be breaking down technical challenges that haven’t been done before in healthcare, we need you to be extremely product minded with every line of code you write\n\n - Iterating quickly: ship, learn from real usage, and refine to make the experience better each time.\n\n\n\nRequirements\n\n - Startup engineering experience where you influenced what to build, not just how to build it\n   \n   - Bonus: you’ve built something from 0 → 1\n\n - A track record of building and shipping full-stack features end-to-end\n\n - Ability to turn messy or unclear problems into a clear plan\n\n - Comfortable working across frontend and backend (perfection in both not required)\n\n - Strong product judgment - within a clear product direction\n\n - Focus on how people actually use the product, not just code elegance\n\n - Fast iteration based on feedback and metrics\n\n - Comfortable working in a domain with hard constraints and complex real-world edge cases\n\n - Proactive about getting feedback from customers on what you ship\n\nYou don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.\n\n\n\nHow you'll be compensated\n\n - Salary: £90K - £130K + equity \n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"£90K – £130K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"£90K - £130K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3eb83552-bcdd-461d-bbda-89bc4c6548f5","tierSummary":"£90K – £130K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d7a8fb4e-c1d0-4e7a-9598-8f141bded953","summary":"£90K – £130K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"GBP","minValue":90000,"maxValue":130000},{"id":"6031b95e-b4f5-4f7b-b49f-5b8b8c1b73f2","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"GBP","minValue":90000,"maxValue":130000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e1fc1b0c-7e17-467c-977b-947c509debb0","title":"Product Engineer, Support","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EDT / EST (US East Coast only)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-06T15:10:04.110+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/e1fc1b0c-7e17-467c-977b-947c509debb0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/e1fc1b0c-7e17-467c-977b-947c509debb0/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Short on time? </strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who you are:</strong> A support-first, customer-driven problem solver with strong technical instincts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> $90K - $130K + equity (based on experience and location)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time zone:</strong> Eastern Time Zone</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why we need this role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction powers modern healthcare companies through clean, reliable APIs. Our customers expect fast and accurate answers because they’re building patient-facing products that can’t break.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer obsessed:</strong> You like helping people unblock real problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical at the core:</strong> You’re comfortable reading code and navigating logs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support-minded:</strong> You see support as a craft, not a stepping stone</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Impact-focused:</strong> You care about getting to the real root of a problem, not just the quickest workaround.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for an engineer who loves working directly with customers, investigating complex escalations, and delivering solutions that unblock customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who you’ll be working with</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Eliot, Customer Support Lead</strong> — your manager and partner in building world-class support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Andy, Product Engineer (Support)</strong> — your peer, working daily in code and logs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The wider engineering, product, sales and ops teams — we’re ~35 people, flat and collaborative</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll sit at the centre of how the company operates.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate and diagnose technical issues</p></li></ol><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Trace issues through logs and our services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand and reproduce errors to find the root cause</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share clear updates with customers and engineers</p></li></ul><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\" start=\"2\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Think like an engineer, act like a support specialist</p></li></ol><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Read code to spot where things break</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI tools to speed up debugging</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make small fixes when appropriate, and escalate when needed</p></li></ul><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\" start=\"3\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver a great customer experience</p></li></ol><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with users from senior engineers to non-technical operators</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adjust your communication based on the audience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond quickly with accurate, thoughtful answers</p></li></ul><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\" start=\"4\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve our documentation, tooling &amp; processes</p></li></ol><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clear docs that reduce repeat questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build small tools or scripts to speed up your workflow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flag recurring issues and suggest improvements</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We're especially interested in candidates with an engineering background who've moved into a support or customer-facing technical role.</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You genuinely enjoy helping people.</strong> Unblocking customers gives you energy — support is something you take pride in.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re mission-driven.</strong> Building technology that improves healthcare matters to you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re a technical problem solver.</strong> You like digging into complex issues, tracing through systems and thinking on your feet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re comfortable in startup environments.</strong> Things move quickly, not everything is defined, and you help bring clarity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You communicate clearly.</strong> You can explain technical things in a way that makes sense for whoever you’re speaking with.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’re comfortable with code.</strong> You’ve spent a couple of years writing or debugging Python and can work through unfamiliar codebases confidently.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How you’ll get to know us</strong></p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Initial call - 30 minutes with Lyn, Technical Recruiter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behavioural and Technical interview - 60 minutes with Eliot and Andy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical interview (live debugging pair programming) - 60 minutes with one of our Engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid trial day - learn what it would be like to work here and meet the rest of the team</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What is the current compensation package</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90K - $130K </p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\n\nShort on time? \n\n - Who you are: A support-first, customer-driven problem solver with strong technical instincts\n\n - Salary: $90K - $130K + equity (based on experience and location)\n\n - Time zone: Eastern Time Zone\n   \n   \n\nWhy we need this role\n\nJunction powers modern healthcare companies through clean, reliable APIs. Our customers expect fast and accurate answers because they’re building patient-facing products that can’t break.\n\n - Customer obsessed: You like helping people unblock real problems\n\n - Technical at the core: You’re comfortable reading code and navigating logs\n\n - Support-minded: You see support as a craft, not a stepping stone\n\n - Impact-focused: You care about getting to the real root of a problem, not just the quickest workaround.\n\nThis role is for an engineer who loves working directly with customers, investigating complex escalations, and delivering solutions that unblock customers.\n\n\n\nWho you’ll be working with\n\n - Eliot, Customer Support Lead — your manager and partner in building world-class support\n\n - Andy, Product Engineer (Support) — your peer, working daily in code and logs\n\n - The wider engineering, product, sales and ops teams — we’re ~35 people, flat and collaborative\n\nYou’ll sit at the centre of how the company operates.\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll be doing day to day\n\n 1. Investigate and diagnose technical issues\n\n - Trace issues through logs and our services\n\n - Understand and reproduce errors to find the root cause\n\n - Share clear updates with customers and engineers\n\n 2. Think like an engineer, act like a support specialist\n\n - Read code to spot where things break\n\n - Use AI tools to speed up debugging\n\n - Make small fixes when appropriate, and escalate when needed\n\n 3. Deliver a great customer experience\n\n - Work with users from senior engineers to non-technical operators\n\n - Adjust your communication based on the audience\n\n - Respond quickly with accurate, thoughtful answers\n\n 4. Improve our documentation, tooling & processes\n\n - Write clear docs that reduce repeat questions\n\n - Build small tools or scripts to speed up your workflow\n\n - Flag recurring issues and suggest improvements\n\n\n\nWho you are\n\nWe're especially interested in candidates with an engineering background who've moved into a support or customer-facing technical role.\n\n - You genuinely enjoy helping people. Unblocking customers gives you energy — support is something you take pride in.\n\n - You’re mission-driven. Building technology that improves healthcare matters to you.\n\n - You’re a technical problem solver. You like digging into complex issues, tracing through systems and thinking on your feet.\n\n - You’re comfortable in startup environments. Things move quickly, not everything is defined, and you help bring clarity.\n\n - You communicate clearly. You can explain technical things in a way that makes sense for whoever you’re speaking with.\n\n - You’re comfortable with code. You’ve spent a couple of years writing or debugging Python and can work through unfamiliar codebases confidently.\n\n\n\nHow you’ll get to know us\n\n 1. Initial call - 30 minutes with Lyn, Technical Recruiter\n\n 2. Behavioural and Technical interview - 60 minutes with Eliot and Andy\n\n 3. Technical interview (live debugging pair programming) - 60 minutes with one of our Engineers\n\n 4. Paid trial day - learn what it would be like to work here and meet the rest of the team\n\n\n\nWhat is the current compensation package\n\n - $90K - $130K \n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$90K – $130K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$90K - $130K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"3264a809-103c-41d4-b40c-19d5c484501d","tierSummary":"$90K – $130K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ad4ffcbe-618c-47ea-b2a9-8fd26721229c","summary":"$90K – $130K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":90000,"maxValue":130000},{"id":"e074a4e1-92c3-4fb3-91ac-5335b9b294ca","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":90000,"maxValue":130000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"e0018853-61d1-4749-9cb4-742032bea4db","title":"Account Executive","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City Metro (Remote)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-10-08T10:50:01.560+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/e0018853-61d1-4749-9cb4-742032bea4db","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/e0018853-61d1-4749-9cb4-742032bea4db/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> An Account Executive who thrives in early-stage environments and cares deeply about fixing healthcare. You're comfortable taking full ownership of pipeline generation, deal progression, and closing with SMBs and Enterprise customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> Team of 4 AE's with support from an SDR team of 2 (and growing!)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary: </strong>$120-140K base, $240-285K OTE</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Metric ownership:</strong> New business ARR + deal velocity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>New York City metro with two days per week in our co-working space for the first three months, and remotely from then on</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why we need this role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As we enter our next phase of growth, we’re hiring our next Account Executive alongside <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/brad-ruzicka/\">Brad</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kendall-duboc-2052a7108/\">Kendall</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/in/patrick-lohuis-5a623374/?skipRedirect=true\">Patrick,</a> and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicholas-rittersbach-pt-dpt-cscs-6775ba108/\">Nick</a> to accelerate new business revenue, build repeatable sales motions, and partner closely with our customers to deliver transformational impact in healthcare. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a quota-carrying role reporting to our Head of Commercial, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/estepansky/\">Eric</a> working alongside our SDRs, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-layman-1484b71a3/\">Ryan</a> and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/anthony-madubuonwu/\">Anthony</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generating and managing pipeline through outbound prospecting, networking, and creative sourcing, partnering with the SDR team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Running high-quality discovery calls to deeply understand customer problems and align Junction’s solution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Driving complex multi-stakeholder deals to close across enterprise teams in healthcare</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handling objections with resilience and empathy, always focused on ethical selling and long-term relationships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Negotiating terms and structuring deals that create value for both Junction and our customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partnering closely with product and customer success to make handoffs smooth and customer value delivery</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What makes you a great fit</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 3+ years experience selling to SMBs + enterprise customers. Selling into healthcare customers isn't mandatory, but your passion for it is! </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re a driven hunter who thrives on building pipeline and closing new business in fast-moving environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You believe in ethical, consultative selling — building trust with customers while holding the line for the company</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You love solving complex problems with technology, and can translate product capabilities into clear value for healthcare stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re a natural relationship builder, able to influence clinicians, execs, and operators alike</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You take ownership and accountability, rallying teams to find solutions and always focusing on delivering real customer impact.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\n\n\nSHORT ON TIME? TL;DR\n\n - You: An Account Executive who thrives in early-stage environments and cares deeply about fixing healthcare. You're comfortable taking full ownership of pipeline generation, deal progression, and closing with SMBs and Enterprise customers\n\n - Us: Team of 4 AE's with support from an SDR team of 2 (and growing!)\n\n - Salary: $120-140K base, $240-285K OTE\n\n - Metric ownership: New business ARR + deal velocity\n\n - Location: New York City metro with two days per week in our co-working space for the first three months, and remotely from then on\n\n\nWHY WE NEED THIS ROLE\n\nAs we enter our next phase of growth, we’re hiring our next Account Executive alongside Brad https://www.linkedin.com/in/brad-ruzicka/, Kendall https://www.linkedin.com/in/kendall-duboc-2052a7108/, Patrick, http://linkedin.com/in/patrick-lohuis-5a623374/?skipRedirect=true and Nick https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicholas-rittersbach-pt-dpt-cscs-6775ba108/ to accelerate new business revenue, build repeatable sales motions, and partner closely with our customers to deliver transformational impact in healthcare. \n\nThis is a quota-carrying role reporting to our Head of Commercial, Eric https://www.linkedin.com/in/estepansky/ working alongside our SDRs, Ryan https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-layman-1484b71a3/ and Anthony https://www.linkedin.com/in/anthony-madubuonwu/.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE DOING DAY TO DAY\n\n - Generating and managing pipeline through outbound prospecting, networking, and creative sourcing, partnering with the SDR team\n\n - Running high-quality discovery calls to deeply understand customer problems and align Junction’s solution\n\n - Driving complex multi-stakeholder deals to close across enterprise teams in healthcare\n\n - Handling objections with resilience and empathy, always focused on ethical selling and long-term relationships\n\n - Negotiating terms and structuring deals that create value for both Junction and our customers\n\n - Partnering closely with product and customer success to make handoffs smooth and customer value delivery\n\n\nWHAT MAKES YOU A GREAT FIT\n\n - You have 3+ years experience selling to SMBs + enterprise customers. Selling into healthcare customers isn't mandatory, but your passion for it is! \n\n - You’re a driven hunter who thrives on building pipeline and closing new business in fast-moving environments\n\n - You believe in ethical, consultative selling — building trust with customers while holding the line for the company\n\n - You love solving complex problems with technology, and can translate product capabilities into clear value for healthcare stakeholders\n\n - You’re a natural relationship builder, able to influence clinicians, execs, and operators alike\n\n - You take ownership and accountability, rallying teams to find solutions and always focusing on delivering real customer impact.\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity • $144K Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $140K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ea94eb33-561f-4682-a841-8f13535fc30d","tierSummary":"$120K – $140K • Offers Equity • $144K Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"bd704a7d-6e14-47c3-98e3-0214fe2066fe","summary":"$120K – $140K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"id":"2ac2b431-f7be-446a-b41f-dd9ddd9b0127","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"cbde859f-2ca3-4e20-b2c2-6e1530b2d41f","summary":"$144K Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":144000,"maxValue":144000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":140000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":144000,"maxValue":144000}]}},{"id":"e469b3a2-038b-4830-8c45-506195f67e49","title":"Technical Recruiter","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"GMT / BST (UK, Portugal, Ireland)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-30T08:40:45.146+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/e469b3a2-038b-4830-8c45-506195f67e49","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/e469b3a2-038b-4830-8c45-506195f67e49/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> Technical recruiter who's built engineering and product teams at Series A+ startups</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> Team of 50, scaling our engineering org, roles including Engineering, Design, Data and Product</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> £65,000 – £90,000 + equity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The salary range shown is intentionally broad to reflect the range of skills and levels that we are open to for this role.</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Fully remote within GMT timezone</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why we need you</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our current team is small and we want to triple it this year. The ambitious part isn't the number — it's finding the right people. People who want to work on hard, interesting problems and actually change something in the world.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'd join a small People &amp; Talent team: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/danielle-rouse-b4b816217/\">Dani</a>, who looks after People Ops; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-hayworth-126b27b1/\">Nicole</a>, who owns all business recruitment; and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sherlynvallet/\">Lyn</a>, who you'd report to and who's been running technical hiring until now. We want someone to take all of technical hiring and put 100% of their energy into it — building pipeline, building a network, caring about every hire we make.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you'll be doing day to day</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Run technical hiring end-to-end:</strong> from first convo to offer, you’re managing multiple roles at a time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Source like it matters:</strong> outbound is core - you’ll be consistently building pipeline. Junction isn’t a household name, so your message needs to stand out.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build our network in European eng:</strong> we want to be known, you'll help us build it up — through content, community, intros, events, whatever works.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep momentum:</strong> chase feedback, unblock decisions, and keep great candidates moving through the process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner closely with hiring managers:</strong> get clear on what we actually need, build sensible interview plans, and keep the bar high.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Treat candidates well:</strong> fast process, clear comms, even a \"no\" should feel respectful of their time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tighten how we hire:</strong> we've got the base — you'll help sharpen scorecards, calibration, and feedback loops. Just enough structure to make good decisions without slowing everyone down.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Feedback what you're seeing with data:</strong> comp expectations, candidate feedback, where we're losing people, and what we should change.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical recruiting experience:</strong> you've hired senior talent at an early-stage company at a high bar. You can hold a real conversation about the problem space and get them excited about it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High-agency operator:</strong> you don't wait around. You figure it out, follow through, and keep things moving.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>In it to build something: y</strong>ou want ownership, you want the responsibility, and you want to look back in two years and point at the team you helped build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Care about every hire:</strong> we're tackling an ambitious problem and every hire shapes the trajectory of the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sourcing-first mindset:</strong> you actually like outbound and get energy from it. You know which companies have great teams, what they're working on, and what their engineering culture is like.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong judgment:</strong> you know what great looks like, and you can back up your call with reasoning.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What this role isn't</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You don't want to source:</strong> outbound is a big part of the job, even with a pipeline in place.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You want a fully polished process on day one:</strong> the foundation is good, but there's still work to do on calibration, brand, and network-building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You prefer high-volume recruiting:</strong> we care more about great hires than speed for the sake of it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You want to recruit across every function:</strong> this role is focused on technical roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're looking for a people manager role:</strong> this is an individual contributor role, you'll be hands-on in the work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How you'll be compensated</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">£65,000 - £90,000 + equity</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\nShort on time? TL;DR\n\n - You: Technical recruiter who's built engineering and product teams at Series A+ startups\n\n - Us: Team of 50, scaling our engineering org, roles including Engineering, Design, Data and Product\n\n - Salary: £65,000 – £90,000 + equity\n   \n   The salary range shown is intentionally broad to reflect the range of skills and levels that we are open to for this role.\n\n - Location: Fully remote within GMT timezone\n\n\n\nWhy we need you\n\nOur current team is small and we want to triple it this year. The ambitious part isn't the number — it's finding the right people. People who want to work on hard, interesting problems and actually change something in the world.\n\nYou'd join a small People & Talent team: Dani https://www.linkedin.com/in/danielle-rouse-b4b816217/, who looks after People Ops; Nicole https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-hayworth-126b27b1/, who owns all business recruitment; and Lyn https://www.linkedin.com/in/sherlynvallet/, who you'd report to and who's been running technical hiring until now. We want someone to take all of technical hiring and put 100% of their energy into it — building pipeline, building a network, caring about every hire we make.\n\n\n\nWhat you'll be doing day to day\n\n - Run technical hiring end-to-end: from first convo to offer, you’re managing multiple roles at a time.\n\n - Source like it matters: outbound is core - you’ll be consistently building pipeline. Junction isn’t a household name, so your message needs to stand out.\n\n - Build our network in European eng: we want to be known, you'll help us build it up — through content, community, intros, events, whatever works.\n\n - Keep momentum: chase feedback, unblock decisions, and keep great candidates moving through the process.\n\n - Partner closely with hiring managers: get clear on what we actually need, build sensible interview plans, and keep the bar high.\n\n - Treat candidates well: fast process, clear comms, even a \"no\" should feel respectful of their time.\n\n - Tighten how we hire: we've got the base — you'll help sharpen scorecards, calibration, and feedback loops. Just enough structure to make good decisions without slowing everyone down.\n\n - Feedback what you're seeing with data: comp expectations, candidate feedback, where we're losing people, and what we should change.\n\nRequirements\n\n - Technical recruiting experience: you've hired senior talent at an early-stage company at a high bar. You can hold a real conversation about the problem space and get them excited about it.\n\n - High-agency operator: you don't wait around. You figure it out, follow through, and keep things moving.\n\n - In it to build something: you want ownership, you want the responsibility, and you want to look back in two years and point at the team you helped build.\n\n - Care about every hire: we're tackling an ambitious problem and every hire shapes the trajectory of the business.\n\n - Sourcing-first mindset: you actually like outbound and get energy from it. You know which companies have great teams, what they're working on, and what their engineering culture is like.\n\n - Strong judgment: you know what great looks like, and you can back up your call with reasoning.\n\nWhat this role isn't\n\n - You don't want to source: outbound is a big part of the job, even with a pipeline in place.\n\n - You want a fully polished process on day one: the foundation is good, but there's still work to do on calibration, brand, and network-building.\n\n - You prefer high-volume recruiting: we care more about great hires than speed for the sake of it.\n\n - You want to recruit across every function: this role is focused on technical roles.\n\n - You're looking for a people manager role: this is an individual contributor role, you'll be hands-on in the work.\n\n\n\nHow you'll be compensated\n\n - £65,000 - £90,000 + equity\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"£65K – £80K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"£65K - £80K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"ed2363a9-0046-4c1a-bbff-bebb45363bc9","tierSummary":"£65K – £80K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ffabdb3e-69c0-4e63-80af-40d51b44443c","summary":"£65K – £80K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"GBP","minValue":65000,"maxValue":80000},{"id":"28596bbc-d508-4693-94ea-b8b7857a9317","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"GBP","minValue":65000,"maxValue":80000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"afce6da5-dec5-484f-845c-12f1c0afa504","title":"Customer Success Manager (Proactive Posting)","department":"Customer Success ","team":"Customer Success ","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EDT / EST (US East Coast only)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T17:25:11.541+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/afce6da5-dec5-484f-845c-12f1c0afa504","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/afce6da5-dec5-484f-845c-12f1c0afa504/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Read this first: this is a proactive posting. The role isn't open today.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We expect to hire a CSM in the future, we just don't have the headcount signed off yet. Rather than wait and then scramble, we're putting the role out early to meet people we'd want to move quickly quickly with when it does open.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>That means a slower timeline than a normal application and no guarantee at the end of it. If that's not worth your time right now, we completely get it.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You: </strong>A high-agency CSM who makes things happen without being asked, is comfortable in commercial conversations, and gets genuinely energized by a technically complex product in a mission-driven space</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us: </strong>A CS team of 6 managing ~40 accounts each, scaling into new segments and raising the bar on how we serve customers</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary: </strong>$120,000 – $150,000 base + bonus + equity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location: </strong>Fully remote (US EST timezone required)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why we need you</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our customer base spans digital health platforms, wearable companies, and health systems – and we’re growing fast in all three. Our CS team is great, but we’re stretched - so we’re on the path to make shifts. The reactive work gets done — onboarding questions, troubleshooting, support coordination. The proactive work is where we’re falling behind: running useful QBRs, spotting expansion opportunities, and catching churn risks early.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This hire is about adding someone with real horsepower. You’ll own a focused book of business – primarily in our digital health segment – from onboarding all the way through renewal and expansion. You’re comfortable in commercial conversations: talking about pricing, pushing on upsell opportunities, and making the case for value when a customer is on the fence. You adapt your approach depending on who you’re talking to – a technical founder needs a completely different conversation than a head of ops, and you can tell the difference quickly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll also need to genuinely enjoy learning how things work. Junction’s product is technical – APIs, data integrations, health data workflows – and the best person for this role is curious about that, not intimidated by it. You’ll work closely with our CS Leader and feed directly into product and engineering with what you’re hearing from customers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own a portfolio of 25–40 accounts across our digital health and mid-market segment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run onboarding for new customers and get them to their first meaningful milestone as quickly as possible</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct quarterly business reviews that are actually useful – not just status updates, but conversations that move things forward</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively identify upsell and cross-sell opportunities and work with our sales team to close them</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a real pulse on account health – usage data, engagement signals, renewal risk – and get ahead of problems before they become urgent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the voice of your customers internally. Bring patterns, feedback, and frustrations to product and engineering in a way they can act on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help define what great CS looks like for wearable and digital health customers – this is still evolving and you’ll have a real hand in shaping it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring a point of view on how AI tools can make CS work faster and smarter - we have budget and appetite to build this into how the team operates</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we measure success</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The metrics that matter most for this role:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Renewal rate across your book of business</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expansion revenue from upsells and cross-sells</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Time-to-value (TTV) for new customers – how quickly they hit their first milestone</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customer satisfaction (NPS/CSAT) across your accounts</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High agency:</strong> You don’t wait to be told what needs doing. You spot problems, form a view, and act. You have examples of things you went after in a previous role that nobody asked you to do.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commercial confidence:</strong> You’re comfortable having pricing and renewal conversations directly. You know how to make the case for value, push on upsell opportunities, and hold a number without hiding behind ‘I’ll loop in sales.’</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Adaptability:</strong> You read the room quickly and flex your approach. A technical founder and a VP of operations need completely different conversations, and you know how to have both.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical curiosity:</strong> You’ve worked with a technical product – APIs, developer tools, data platforms, or similar – and you actually enjoyed getting into how it works. You have a method for learning things you don’t understand yet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>CS experience:</strong> 3–6 years owning accounts end-to-end. You’ve managed 20–50 accounts at a time and know how to stay on top of them without things slipping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Early-stage background:</strong> You’ve worked at a Seed through Series C company. Things were ambiguous, processes were still being built, and that energized you rather than frustrated you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring a point of view on how AI tools can make CS work faster and smarter — we have budget and appetite to build this into how the team operates.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>You don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What this role isn’t</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You want a fully defined playbook from day one – we’re still building ours and you’ll have a hand in writing it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You prefer reactive CS – most of the value in this role comes from going out and making things happen, not responding to inbound</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re not comfortable owning commercial conversations – renewals, upsells, and pricing discussions are part of the job, not something to escalate away</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You want to specialize – you’ll touch onboarding, retention, expansion, and internal feedback loops, often in the same week</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technical products make you uncomfortable – Junction’s API-first platform requires genuine curiosity about how things work, not just a surface-level understanding</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\nRead this first: this is a proactive posting. The role isn't open today.\n\nWe expect to hire a CSM in the future, we just don't have the headcount signed off yet. Rather than wait and then scramble, we're putting the role out early to meet people we'd want to move quickly quickly with when it does open.\n\nThat means a slower timeline than a normal application and no guarantee at the end of it. If that's not worth your time right now, we completely get it.\n\n\n\nShort on time? TL;DR\n\nYou: A high-agency CSM who makes things happen without being asked, is comfortable in commercial conversations, and gets genuinely energized by a technically complex product in a mission-driven space\n\nUs: A CS team of 6 managing ~40 accounts each, scaling into new segments and raising the bar on how we serve customers\n\nSalary: $120,000 – $150,000 base + bonus + equity\n\nLocation: Fully remote (US EST timezone required)\n\n\n\nWhy we need you\n\nOur customer base spans digital health platforms, wearable companies, and health systems – and we’re growing fast in all three. Our CS team is great, but we’re stretched - so we’re on the path to make shifts. The reactive work gets done — onboarding questions, troubleshooting, support coordination. The proactive work is where we’re falling behind: running useful QBRs, spotting expansion opportunities, and catching churn risks early.\n\nThis hire is about adding someone with real horsepower. You’ll own a focused book of business – primarily in our digital health segment – from onboarding all the way through renewal and expansion. You’re comfortable in commercial conversations: talking about pricing, pushing on upsell opportunities, and making the case for value when a customer is on the fence. You adapt your approach depending on who you’re talking to – a technical founder needs a completely different conversation than a head of ops, and you can tell the difference quickly.\n\nYou’ll also need to genuinely enjoy learning how things work. Junction’s product is technical – APIs, data integrations, health data workflows – and the best person for this role is curious about that, not intimidated by it. You’ll work closely with our CS Leader and feed directly into product and engineering with what you’re hearing from customers.\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll be doing day to day\n\n - Own a portfolio of 25–40 accounts across our digital health and mid-market segment\n\n - Run onboarding for new customers and get them to their first meaningful milestone as quickly as possible\n\n - Conduct quarterly business reviews that are actually useful – not just status updates, but conversations that move things forward\n\n - Proactively identify upsell and cross-sell opportunities and work with our sales team to close them\n\n - Build a real pulse on account health – usage data, engagement signals, renewal risk – and get ahead of problems before they become urgent\n\n - Be the voice of your customers internally. Bring patterns, feedback, and frustrations to product and engineering in a way they can act on\n\n - Help define what great CS looks like for wearable and digital health customers – this is still evolving and you’ll have a real hand in shaping it\n\n - Bring a point of view on how AI tools can make CS work faster and smarter - we have budget and appetite to build this into how the team operates\n\n\n\nHow we measure success\n\nThe metrics that matter most for this role:\n\n - Renewal rate across your book of business\n\n - Expansion revenue from upsells and cross-sells\n\n - Time-to-value (TTV) for new customers – how quickly they hit their first milestone\n\n - Customer satisfaction (NPS/CSAT) across your accounts\n\n\n\nWhat we’re looking for\n\n - High agency: You don’t wait to be told what needs doing. You spot problems, form a view, and act. You have examples of things you went after in a previous role that nobody asked you to do.\n\n - Commercial confidence: You’re comfortable having pricing and renewal conversations directly. You know how to make the case for value, push on upsell opportunities, and hold a number without hiding behind ‘I’ll loop in sales.’\n\n - Adaptability: You read the room quickly and flex your approach. A technical founder and a VP of operations need completely different conversations, and you know how to have both.\n\n - Technical curiosity: You’ve worked with a technical product – APIs, developer tools, data platforms, or similar – and you actually enjoyed getting into how it works. You have a method for learning things you don’t understand yet.\n\n - CS experience: 3–6 years owning accounts end-to-end. You’ve managed 20–50 accounts at a time and know how to stay on top of them without things slipping.\n\n - Early-stage background: You’ve worked at a Seed through Series C company. Things were ambiguous, processes were still being built, and that energized you rather than frustrated you.\n\n - Bring a point of view on how AI tools can make CS work faster and smarter — we have budget and appetite to build this into how the team operates.\n\nYou don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.\n\n\n\nWhat this role isn’t\n\n - You want a fully defined playbook from day one – we’re still building ours and you’ll have a hand in writing it\n\n - You prefer reactive CS – most of the value in this role comes from going out and making things happen, not responding to inbound\n\n - You’re not comfortable owning commercial conversations – renewals, upsells, and pricing discussions are part of the job, not something to escalate away\n\n - You want to specialize – you’ll touch onboarding, retention, expansion, and internal feedback loops, often in the same week\n\n - Technical products make you uncomfortable – Junction’s API-first platform requires genuine curiosity about how things work, not just a surface-level understanding\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $150K • Offers Equity • $20K – $30K Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $150K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"9bd10950-0d92-4d44-a558-0852ce995ffa","tierSummary":"$120K – $150K • Offers Equity • $20K – $30K Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e7bea7d6-7f9b-48b1-a46a-a2b6d4455a9a","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"253c2549-ad37-401a-996e-bf6f10daa366","summary":"$120K – $150K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":150000},{"id":"d4f9c3a2-9cda-488e-a5dc-8c3e00e084c2","summary":"$20K – $30K Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20000,"maxValue":30000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":150000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":20000,"maxValue":30000}]}},{"id":"634c5cb8-e98b-4421-8da4-bc55db392f74","title":"Engineering Manager","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"GMT / BST (UK, Portugal, Ireland)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"United Kingdom (Remote)","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-14T15:41:13.880+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/634c5cb8-e98b-4421-8da4-bc55db392f74","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/634c5cb8-e98b-4421-8da4-bc55db392f74/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><h2><strong>Short on time? </strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> You’ve led experienced engineers, stayed close to the code, and care about the product and the customers using it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ownership / Focus:</strong> You’ll lead a small and growing engineering team, you’ll own its engineering direction, technical delivery, team health and hiring.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How we manage:</strong> We don’t believe in purely pastoral engineering managers. You’ll manage and develop people, but you’ll also ship, unblock, review and make technical decisions alongside them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> £120-£150k + equity (based on experience and location)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Fully remote (GMT). We have one company offsite each year, with possible travel to London every couple of months for team meet-ups.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why we need you</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our engineering team is growing, and we need another Engineering Manager to grow with it. You’ll report to Mark, our Head of Engineering, and work alongside Rui, our other Engineering Manager. You’ll initially take ownership of a small engineering team, working closely with product and other teams to decide what to build and get it shipped.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Junction, engineering management is a technical job. We want our managers close enough to the work to know what’s going on, give good feedback and get involved when needed. But we don’t want you to become the person everyone waits for when something gets difficult.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Six months in, your team should trust you, people outside the team should know where things stand, and the team should be delivering what it says it will.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What you’ll be doing day to day</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the engineering direction, delivery and health of a small team of senior product engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with product on what the team commits to, then make sure it gets delivered.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay close to the code: review PRs, give technical feedback, pair on problems and ship when it makes sense.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unblock the team when decisions are unclear or things go wrong.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Give engineers regular feedback, run useful 1:1s and performance reviews, and actively help them grow in their careers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Notice what’s slowing the team down and fix it, surface problems early and keep the rest of the company clear on what’s happening.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own hiring for your team and play an active role in helping Junction grow.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Requirements</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve led and directly managed experienced software engineers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve stayed technically involved while managing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve owned a team’s delivery, not just its people management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You can give useful technical feedback and make sound calls on engineering trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve worked with product and other teams to turn customer problems into shipped software.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve helped engineers develop through direct feedback, coaching and meaningful opportunities to take on more.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve hired engineers and helped raise the technical or operating standards of a team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>You don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.</em></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve worked at an early-stage or scaling company where managers are expected to manage people and build product.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What this role isn’t</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you want to stay out of the code and spend most of your time in 1:1s, planning and status meetings, it won’t be a good fit.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll have to make tough calls on technical and non-technical topics and own the outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">It isn’t a tech lead role with a few 1:1s either. Developing people, giving difficult feedback, hiring and building a healthy team are core parts of the job.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How you'll be compensated</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\nSHORT ON TIME? \n\n - You: You’ve led experienced engineers, stayed close to the code, and care about the product and the customers using it.\n\n - Ownership / Focus: You’ll lead a small and growing engineering team, you’ll own its engineering direction, technical delivery, team health and hiring.\n\n - How we manage: We don’t believe in purely pastoral engineering managers. You’ll manage and develop people, but you’ll also ship, unblock, review and make technical decisions alongside them.\n\n - Salary: £120-£150k + equity (based on experience and location)\n\n - Location: Fully remote (GMT). We have one company offsite each year, with possible travel to London every couple of months for team meet-ups.\n\n\n\n\nWHY WE NEED YOU\n\nOur engineering team is growing, and we need another Engineering Manager to grow with it. You’ll report to Mark, our Head of Engineering, and work alongside Rui, our other Engineering Manager. You’ll initially take ownership of a small engineering team, working closely with product and other teams to decide what to build and get it shipped.\n\nAt Junction, engineering management is a technical job. We want our managers close enough to the work to know what’s going on, give good feedback and get involved when needed. But we don’t want you to become the person everyone waits for when something gets difficult.\n\nSix months in, your team should trust you, people outside the team should know where things stand, and the team should be delivering what it says it will.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE DOING DAY TO DAY\n\n - Own the engineering direction, delivery and health of a small team of senior product engineers.\n\n - Work with product on what the team commits to, then make sure it gets delivered.\n\n - Stay close to the code: review PRs, give technical feedback, pair on problems and ship when it makes sense.\n\n - Unblock the team when decisions are unclear or things go wrong.\n\n - Give engineers regular feedback, run useful 1:1s and performance reviews, and actively help them grow in their careers.\n\n - Notice what’s slowing the team down and fix it, surface problems early and keep the rest of the company clear on what’s happening.\n\n - Own hiring for your team and play an active role in helping Junction grow.\n\n\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - You’ve led and directly managed experienced software engineers.\n\n - You’ve stayed technically involved while managing\n\n - You’ve owned a team’s delivery, not just its people management.\n\n - You can give useful technical feedback and make sound calls on engineering trade-offs.\n\n - You’ve worked with product and other teams to turn customer problems into shipped software.\n\n - You’ve helped engineers develop through direct feedback, coaching and meaningful opportunities to take on more.\n\n - You’ve hired engineers and helped raise the technical or operating standards of a team.\n\nYou don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.\n\n \n \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - You’ve worked at an early-stage or scaling company where managers are expected to manage people and build product.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT THIS ROLE ISN’T\n\n - If you want to stay out of the code and spend most of your time in 1:1s, planning and status meetings, it won’t be a good fit.\n\n - You’ll have to make tough calls on technical and non-technical topics and own the outcomes\n\n - It isn’t a tech lead role with a few 1:1s either. Developing people, giving difficult feedback, hiring and building a healthy team are core parts of the job.\n\n\n\nHow you'll be compensated\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"£120K – £150K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"£120K - £150K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"707d3696-06ff-4e70-bdfe-63c4323afcd0","tierSummary":"£120K – £150K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6a00842a-9c35-498a-a672-d1cdb85cf6ee","summary":"£120K – £150K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"GBP","minValue":120000,"maxValue":150000},{"id":"c2d5a25a-14da-4656-b571-fcd9cc74362b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"GBP","minValue":120000,"maxValue":150000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"71c37ebb-5896-4c69-967e-0ecd0e75e9c6","title":"Business Development Representative","department":"Sales","team":"Sales","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City Metro (Hybrid)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-02T19:25:05.400+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York City Metro","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City Metro"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/71c37ebb-5896-4c69-967e-0ecd0e75e9c6","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/71c37ebb-5896-4c69-967e-0ecd0e75e9c6/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><h2><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> A systems thinker who builds outbound infrastructure, not just executes it. You think in workflows, iterate on data, and treat outreach as a craft.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ownership:</strong> Top of funnel: account identification, outbound sequencing, signal-based prospecting, and meeting generation</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> A sales team of 7, you’ll be our 3rd BDR</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> $70-80K base + $30K commission at 100% quota (uncapped!)  + equity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> New York City metro with two days per week in our co-working space for the first three months, then remotely from then on</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why we need you</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is scaling aggressively in 2026. We have a proven ICP, a repeatable set of buying signals, and a pipeline of digital health companies that need what we build. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">What we need now is people who can operationalize how we reach them.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This isn't a role where you inherit a playbook and execute. The playbook is still being written — and you'll help write it. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be working closely with <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/estepansky/\">Eric</a>, Head of Sales, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-layman-1484b71a3/\"><u>Ryan</u></a> and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/anthony-madubuonwu/\">Anthony</a>, our current BDRs, building the outbound systems, messaging, and targeting logic that will scale with us as we grow our GTM teams this year.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building and iterating on outbound sequences and enrichment workflows in Clay</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identifying and acting on buying signals: funding rounds, job postings, product launches, exec moves, and category shifts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Researching and prioritizing accounts against our ICP — then figuring out how to reach the right person with the right message</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Writing outbound copy and running experiments: testing subject lines, messaging angles, and ICP-specific value props</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Qualifying prospects and setting discovery meetings with the AE team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What this role is not</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Being transparent matters to us. This role will disappoint you if you're looking for:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A high-volume dialing role.</strong> We don't cold call. Our outreach is deliberate, signal-driven, and channel-agnostic — but it isn't the phone.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A process-follower role.</strong> There's no thick playbook to inherit. You'll be expected to build structure in ambiguous conditions, not wait for it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>A role where activity metrics = success.</strong> We measure quality pipeline. Meetings booked matter; dials made don't.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Who you are</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've built outbound workflows yourself</strong>, not just used them. You can walk through what you built, why, and what problem it solved.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You find tools before your manager suggests them.</strong> You're always looking for what makes you more effective, and you can articulate the impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You think in systems.</strong> When outreach isn't landing, you diagnose before you change and can explain what you tried, what the data showed, and what you did differently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You write well.</strong> Outbound email is a craft. You care about specificity, relevance, and why something would actually matter to the person reading it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've worked in ambiguous environments</strong> and either thrived or actively built the structure around you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior SDR or outbound experience in B2B SaaS or a technical product is preferred. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>A plus if</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience in digital health, healthcare tech, or selling to technical buyers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You're familiar with our ICP — Series A–C digital health companies building consumer-facing health products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've been an early or founding BDR or GTM Associate, where you had to build rather than inherit</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\nSHORT ON TIME? TL;DR\n\nYou: A systems thinker who builds outbound infrastructure, not just executes it. You think in workflows, iterate on data, and treat outreach as a craft.\n\nOwnership: Top of funnel: account identification, outbound sequencing, signal-based prospecting, and meeting generation\n\nUs: A sales team of 7, you’ll be our 3rd BDR\n\nSalary: $70-80K base + $30K commission at 100% quota (uncapped!)  + equity\n\nLocation: New York City metro with two days per week in our co-working space for the first three months, then remotely from then on\n\n\n\n\nWHY WE NEED YOU\n\nJunction is scaling aggressively in 2026. We have a proven ICP, a repeatable set of buying signals, and a pipeline of digital health companies that need what we build. \n\nWhat we need now is people who can operationalize how we reach them.\n\nThis isn't a role where you inherit a playbook and execute. The playbook is still being written — and you'll help write it. \n\nYou'll be working closely with Eric https://www.linkedin.com/in/estepansky/, Head of Sales, Ryan https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-layman-1484b71a3/ and Anthony https://www.linkedin.com/in/anthony-madubuonwu/, our current BDRs, building the outbound systems, messaging, and targeting logic that will scale with us as we grow our GTM teams this year.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE DOING DAY TO DAY\n\n - Building and iterating on outbound sequences and enrichment workflows in Clay\n\n - Identifying and acting on buying signals: funding rounds, job postings, product launches, exec moves, and category shifts\n\n - Researching and prioritizing accounts against our ICP — then figuring out how to reach the right person with the right message\n\n - Writing outbound copy and running experiments: testing subject lines, messaging angles, and ICP-specific value props\n\n - Qualifying prospects and setting discovery meetings with the AE team\n\n\n\n\nWHAT THIS ROLE IS NOT\n\nBeing transparent matters to us. This role will disappoint you if you're looking for:\n\n - A high-volume dialing role. We don't cold call. Our outreach is deliberate, signal-driven, and channel-agnostic — but it isn't the phone.\n\n - A process-follower role. There's no thick playbook to inherit. You'll be expected to build structure in ambiguous conditions, not wait for it.\n\n - A role where activity metrics = success. We measure quality pipeline. Meetings booked matter; dials made don't.\n\n\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - You've built outbound workflows yourself, not just used them. You can walk through what you built, why, and what problem it solved.\n\n - You find tools before your manager suggests them. You're always looking for what makes you more effective, and you can articulate the impact.\n\n - You think in systems. When outreach isn't landing, you diagnose before you change and can explain what you tried, what the data showed, and what you did differently.\n\n - You write well. Outbound email is a craft. You care about specificity, relevance, and why something would actually matter to the person reading it.\n\n - You've worked in ambiguous environments and either thrived or actively built the structure around you.\n\n - Prior SDR or outbound experience in B2B SaaS or a technical product is preferred. \n\n\n\n\nA PLUS IF\n\n - You have experience in digital health, healthcare tech, or selling to technical buyers\n\n - You're familiar with our ICP — Series A–C digital health companies building consumer-facing health products\n\n - You've been an early or founding BDR or GTM Associate, where you had to build rather than inherit\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$70K – $80K • Offers Equity • $30K Commission","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$70K - $80K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"797ad53b-cfb4-42fc-84b3-8662dcdb5959","tierSummary":"$70K – $80K • Offers Equity • $30K Commission","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"cca76a6a-4e5d-45fe-b801-13cb32230267","summary":"$70K – $80K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":70000,"maxValue":80000},{"id":"04296426-8181-4b2f-999f-ea4d3e912069","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"899ca5a4-f7b3-4efc-bf20-5ef35cd57522","summary":"$30K Commission","compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":30000,"maxValue":30000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":70000,"maxValue":80000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Commission","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":30000,"maxValue":30000}]}},{"id":"9daf527a-586e-4c3b-a0b6-85fcd95b5681","title":"External Referral Form","department":"All functions","team":"All functions","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote first - Western European + Eastern time zones","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T09:58:20.628+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":null,"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/9daf527a-586e-4c3b-a0b6-85fcd95b5681","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/9daf527a-586e-4c3b-a0b6-85fcd95b5681/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><h1><strong>Refer a candidate to Junction to earn a $5,000 referral bonus!</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Submit your referral by clicking the 'application' tab and sharing more information with us. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>You can find out more details about our referral program </strong><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.notion.so/junction-api/External-Referral-Program-348d9955818e80148552efc101fb951d\"><strong>here</strong></a><strong>. </strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A few important notes:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks currently living in the following timezones:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">EST</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">GMT</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">PHT (Philippines)</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not offer visa sponsorship</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our referral bonus is paid out when your referral successfully passes three months of employment at Junction</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What is the current compensation package</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\nREFER A CANDIDATE TO JUNCTION TO EARN A $5,000 REFERRAL BONUS!\n\nSubmit your referral by clicking the 'application' tab and sharing more information with us. \n\n\n\n\nYOU CAN FIND OUT MORE DETAILS ABOUT OUR REFERRAL PROGRAM HERE https://www.notion.so/junction-api/External-Referral-Program-348d9955818e80148552efc101fb951d. \n\n\n\nA few important notes:\n\n - We only hire folks currently living in the following timezones:\n   \n   - EST\n   \n   - GMT\n   \n   - PHT (Philippines)\n\n - We do not offer visa sponsorship\n\n - Our referral bonus is paid out when your referral successfully passes three months of employment at Junction\n\n\n\nWhat is the current compensation package\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ba5782e5-e728-4b30-a4b8-892a7e39cc81","title":"Business Recruiter","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EDT / EST (US East Coast only)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-03T15:39:07.637+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/ba5782e5-e728-4b30-a4b8-892a7e39cc81","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/ba5782e5-e728-4b30-a4b8-892a7e39cc81/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> Business recruiter who’s excited by sourcing-heavy roles + being part of building a hiring function early</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> Team of ~50 (Team of 3 in People &amp; Talent)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> $130,000 - $180,000+ equity</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>The salary range shown is intentionally broad to reflect the range of skills and levels that we are open to for this role.</em></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Fully remote (EST timezone only)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why we need you</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’ve built strong foundations, but we’re still scrappy. Now we’re entering our next phase: scaling each team from its early “founding” stage into something much bigger. That means hiring broadly across Operations &amp; Support — and in healthcare, that list runs long, with Operations being the biggest and most immediate need. These are the roles that keep the company running, keep customers and patients trusted and cared for, and give everyone else the room to grow.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is our chance to level up recruiting across the company: not just filling roles, but shaping how we hire: the story we tell, the bar we set, and the experience candidates remember.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'd join a small People &amp; Talent team: <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/danielle-rouse-b4b816217/\">Dani</a>, who looks after People Ops; <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-hayworth-126b27b1/\">Nicole</a>, who owns GTM recruitment; and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sherlynvallet/\">Lyn</a>, who you'd report to and who's been running business hiring until now. We want someone to take all of business hiring — Operations &amp; Support, and everything in between and put 100% of their energy into it: building pipeline, building a network, caring about every hire we make.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a builder role, there's no polished machine to inherit here — you're building the pipeline, the process from scratch.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own business hiring end to end — Operations &amp; Support, and whatever else the business needs, with Operations making up the bulk of it given the nature of healthcare. You'll become the expert — know who's great in this space, build the relationships before you need them, and use that network to move fast. And you'll partner closely with hiring managers to keep the bar high as we scale.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Run business hiring end-to-end:</strong> from first convo to offer, you’re managing multiple roles at a time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Source like it matters:</strong> outbound is core - you’ll be consistently building pipeline. Junction isn’t a household name, so your message needs to stand out.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Build our network in the healthcare tech industry:</strong> we want to be known, you'll help us build it up — through content, community, intros, events, whatever works.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep momentum:</strong> chase feedback, unblock decisions, and keep great candidates moving through the process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner closely with hiring managers:</strong> get clear on what we actually need, build sensible interview plans, and keep the bar high.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Treat candidates well:</strong> fast process, clear comms, even a \"no\" should feel respectful of their time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Tighten how we hire:</strong> we've got the base — you'll help sharpen scorecards, calibration, and feedback loops. Just enough structure to make good decisions without slowing everyone down.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Feedback what you're seeing with data:</strong> comp expectations, candidate feedback, where we're losing people, and what we should change.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Startup experience:</strong> you've recruited at an early-stage company at a high bar, especially for business roles (Ops, Support and G&amp;A). Things move fast, roles evolve, and you're great with that.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High-agency operator:</strong> you don't wait around, you figure it out, follow through, and keep things moving.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Full-cycle experience:</strong> you can run a hiring process end-to-end and keep a few roles moving at once. Every hire matters to you, they're not a number.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Sourcing-first mindset:</strong> you actually like outbound and don't need inbound to build a strong pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Good with messy roles:</strong> you can hire when the role isn't fully defined yet (a brand-new ops function, a first-of-its-kind Support hire, \"we need someone to build this\").</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Async-native communicator:</strong> you write clearly, keep people aligned across time zones, and don't create meetings for no reason.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong judgment:</strong> you know what great looks like and can explain a clear yes/no without hand-waving.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What this role isn't</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You don't want to source:</strong> outbound is a big part of the job, even with a pipeline in place.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You want a fully polished process on day one:</strong> the foundation is good, but there's still work to do on calibration, brand, and network-building.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're looking for a people manager role:</strong> this is an individual contributor role, you'll be hands-on in the work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>How you'll be compensated</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$130,000 - $180,000+ equity</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\n\nShort on time? TL;DR\n\n - You: Business recruiter who’s excited by sourcing-heavy roles + being part of building a hiring function early\n\n - Us: Team of ~50 (Team of 3 in People & Talent)\n\n - Salary: $130,000 - $180,000+ equity\n   \n   The salary range shown is intentionally broad to reflect the range of skills and levels that we are open to for this role.\n\n - Location: Fully remote (EST timezone only)\n\n\n\nWhy we need you\n\nWe’ve built strong foundations, but we’re still scrappy. Now we’re entering our next phase: scaling each team from its early “founding” stage into something much bigger. That means hiring broadly across Operations & Support — and in healthcare, that list runs long, with Operations being the biggest and most immediate need. These are the roles that keep the company running, keep customers and patients trusted and cared for, and give everyone else the room to grow.\n\nThis role is our chance to level up recruiting across the company: not just filling roles, but shaping how we hire: the story we tell, the bar we set, and the experience candidates remember.\n\nYou'd join a small People & Talent team: Dani https://www.linkedin.com/in/danielle-rouse-b4b816217/, who looks after People Ops; Nicole https://www.linkedin.com/in/nicole-hayworth-126b27b1/, who owns GTM recruitment; and Lyn https://www.linkedin.com/in/sherlynvallet/, who you'd report to and who's been running business hiring until now. We want someone to take all of business hiring — Operations & Support, and everything in between and put 100% of their energy into it: building pipeline, building a network, caring about every hire we make.\n\n\n\nWhat you’ll be doing day to day\n\nThis is a builder role, there's no polished machine to inherit here — you're building the pipeline, the process from scratch.\n\nYou'll own business hiring end to end — Operations & Support, and whatever else the business needs, with Operations making up the bulk of it given the nature of healthcare. You'll become the expert — know who's great in this space, build the relationships before you need them, and use that network to move fast. And you'll partner closely with hiring managers to keep the bar high as we scale.\n\n - Run business hiring end-to-end: from first convo to offer, you’re managing multiple roles at a time.\n\n - Source like it matters: outbound is core - you’ll be consistently building pipeline. Junction isn’t a household name, so your message needs to stand out.\n\n - Build our network in the healthcare tech industry: we want to be known, you'll help us build it up — through content, community, intros, events, whatever works.\n\n - Keep momentum: chase feedback, unblock decisions, and keep great candidates moving through the process.\n\n - Partner closely with hiring managers: get clear on what we actually need, build sensible interview plans, and keep the bar high.\n\n - Treat candidates well: fast process, clear comms, even a \"no\" should feel respectful of their time.\n\n - Tighten how we hire: we've got the base — you'll help sharpen scorecards, calibration, and feedback loops. Just enough structure to make good decisions without slowing everyone down.\n\n - Feedback what you're seeing with data: comp expectations, candidate feedback, where we're losing people, and what we should change.\n\nRequirements\n\n - Startup experience: you've recruited at an early-stage company at a high bar, especially for business roles (Ops, Support and G&A). Things move fast, roles evolve, and you're great with that.\n\n - High-agency operator: you don't wait around, you figure it out, follow through, and keep things moving.\n\n - Full-cycle experience: you can run a hiring process end-to-end and keep a few roles moving at once. Every hire matters to you, they're not a number.\n\n - Sourcing-first mindset: you actually like outbound and don't need inbound to build a strong pipeline.\n\n - Good with messy roles: you can hire when the role isn't fully defined yet (a brand-new ops function, a first-of-its-kind Support hire, \"we need someone to build this\").\n\n - Async-native communicator: you write clearly, keep people aligned across time zones, and don't create meetings for no reason.\n\n - Strong judgment: you know what great looks like and can explain a clear yes/no without hand-waving.\n\nWhat this role isn't\n\n - You don't want to source: outbound is a big part of the job, even with a pipeline in place.\n\n - You want a fully polished process on day one: the foundation is good, but there's still work to do on calibration, brand, and network-building.\n\n - You're looking for a people manager role: this is an individual contributor role, you'll be hands-on in the work.\n\n\n\nHow you'll be compensated\n\n - $130,000 - $180,000+ equity\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$130K – $180K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$130K - $180K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"21eca0c1-1425-4cec-9f65-1e12ae283ad0","tierSummary":"$130K – $180K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"e6414ce0-2e47-46d5-8ba5-461f799fbb60","summary":"$130K – $180K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":180000},{"id":"afb32e0f-e98b-4f7a-afb8-280e0f038c3b","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":130000,"maxValue":180000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"76cce4d7-ba68-4581-a299-c47df850c84e","title":"Operations Associate","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Philippines (Remote)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-16T17:20:36.538+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":null,"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/76cce4d7-ba68-4581-a299-c47df850c84e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/76cce4d7-ba68-4581-a299-c47df850c84e/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><h2><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> A detail-oriented, problem-solving operations professional, ideally with healthcare-related experience, who’s excited to join a technical startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> A fast-growing healthcare technology company based in the US, reshaping how patients access and manage lab testing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Compensation:</strong> $1,500 monthly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote, must be based in the Philippines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Time zone:</strong> We are looking for folks who are comfortable working one of the following schedules (Eastern Time):</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monday-Friday OR Tuesday-Saturday</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8am - 4pm</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">9am - 5pm</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10am - 6pm</p></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><h2><strong>Why we need this role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As we scale, providing seamless lab test processing, vendor coordination, and real-time system monitoring is critical to delivering high-quality healthcare experiences. Our Operations Associates are the backbone of day-to-day service delivery, ensuring patients, labs, and clients are always supported with precision and care.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll be joining a team of 10 Operations Associates, all based in the Philippines, working closely with our global team of 50.</p><h2><strong>What you’ll be owning</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll be working directly with our Lab Ops Team Manager, Jewel, and our Head of Operations <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/aditya-r-shah/\">Aditya,</a> alongside our customer support, customer success, and engineering teams. You will also interact frequently with external vendors, including diagnostic labs and healthcare partners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Given our size and stage, you’ll have exposure across the company and contribute to building the foundations of how we run Operations at scale.</p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing day to day</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Lab Test Management</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Process lab test orders, ensuring timely and accurate delivery of results</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with diagnostic labs, customers, and vendors to resolve lab order or resulting issues</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>System Monitoring &amp; Issue Resolution</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor internal dashboards for system delays or outages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proactively troubleshoot and escalate issues across multiple internal platforms</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer Support &amp; Communication</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide direct support to customers via Slack, email, and internal ticketing systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain SLA standards for response and resolution times</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interact with clients primarily through chat, with occasional voice support</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Support</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist the Operations team with routine tasks to ensure smooth workflow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally to support process improvements and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use internal tools such as Google Docs, Linear, and Slack for communication and task tracking</p></li></ul></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2-5+ years of overall professional work experience working with US-based companies</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backgrounds we especially value: revenue cycle management, medical billing or claims processing, medical coding, clinical data abstraction, lab/diagnostics operations, IT or technical support, systems/NOC monitoring, or vendor/logistics coordination</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience handling medical data or lab results is a huge plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup or small company experience is a strong plus</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills, especially written (B2 English level minimum – business professional)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Problem-solving mindset with the ability to work independently and adapt in a fast-paced environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with remote work environment tools like Slack/Microsoft Teams, Google Workspace, and Linear/Jira</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly pay rate: $1,500</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly health insurance stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Opportunity to attend global company and local team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">One-time stipend to set up your workstation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Annual productivity stipend to spend on learning/courses</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid sick time, public holidays</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Paid overtime and on-call</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work setup: Remote role, must be based in the Philippines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Schedule: We are looking for folks who are comfortable working one of the following schedules (Eastern Time):</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monday-Friday or Tuesday-Saturday</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8am - 4pm</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">9am - 5pm</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10am - 6pm</p></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\nSHORT ON TIME? TL;DR\n\n - You: A detail-oriented, problem-solving operations professional, ideally with healthcare-related experience, who’s excited to join a technical startup\n\n - Us: A fast-growing healthcare technology company based in the US, reshaping how patients access and manage lab testing\n\n - Compensation: $1,500 monthly\n\n - Location: Remote, must be based in the Philippines\n\n - Time zone: We are looking for folks who are comfortable working one of the following schedules (Eastern Time):\n   \n   - Monday-Friday OR Tuesday-Saturday\n     \n     - 8am - 4pm\n     \n     - 9am - 5pm\n     \n     - 10am - 6pm\n\n\nWHY WE NEED THIS ROLE\n\nAs we scale, providing seamless lab test processing, vendor coordination, and real-time system monitoring is critical to delivering high-quality healthcare experiences. Our Operations Associates are the backbone of day-to-day service delivery, ensuring patients, labs, and clients are always supported with precision and care.\n\nYou’ll be joining a team of 10 Operations Associates, all based in the Philippines, working closely with our global team of 50.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE OWNING\n\nYou’ll be working directly with our Lab Ops Team Manager, Jewel, and our Head of Operations Aditya, https://www.linkedin.com/in/aditya-r-shah/ alongside our customer support, customer success, and engineering teams. You will also interact frequently with external vendors, including diagnostic labs and healthcare partners.\n\nGiven our size and stage, you’ll have exposure across the company and contribute to building the foundations of how we run Operations at scale.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL BE DOING DAY TO DAY\n\n - Lab Test Management\n   \n   - Process lab test orders, ensuring timely and accurate delivery of results\n   \n   - Coordinate with diagnostic labs, customers, and vendors to resolve lab order or resulting issues\n\n - System Monitoring & Issue Resolution\n   \n   - Monitor internal dashboards for system delays or outages\n   \n   - Proactively troubleshoot and escalate issues across multiple internal platforms\n\n - Customer Support & Communication\n   \n   - Provide direct support to customers via Slack, email, and internal ticketing systems\n   \n   - Maintain SLA standards for response and resolution times\n   \n   - Interact with clients primarily through chat, with occasional voice support\n\n - Operational Support\n   \n   - Assist the Operations team with routine tasks to ensure smooth workflow\n   \n   - Collaborate cross-functionally to support process improvements and documentation\n   \n   - Use internal tools such as Google Docs, Linear, and Slack for communication and task tracking\n\n\nWHO YOU ARE\n\n - 2-5+ years of overall professional work experience working with US-based companies\n   \n   - Backgrounds we especially value: revenue cycle management, medical billing or claims processing, medical coding, clinical data abstraction, lab/diagnostics operations, IT or technical support, systems/NOC monitoring, or vendor/logistics coordination\n   \n   - Experience handling medical data or lab results is a huge plus\n   \n   - Startup or small company experience is a strong plus\n\n - Excellent communication skills, especially written (B2 English level minimum – business professional)\n\n - Problem-solving mindset with the ability to work independently and adapt in a fast-paced environment\n\n - Familiarity with remote work environment tools like Slack/Microsoft Teams, Google Workspace, and Linear/Jira\n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - Monthly pay rate: $1,500\n\n - Monthly health insurance stipend\n\n - Opportunity to attend global company and local team offsites\n\n - One-time stipend to set up your workstation\n\n - Annual productivity stipend to spend on learning/courses\n\n - Paid sick time, public holidays\n\n - Paid overtime and on-call\n\n - Work setup: Remote role, must be based in the Philippines\n\n - Schedule: We are looking for folks who are comfortable working one of the following schedules (Eastern Time):\n   \n   - Monday-Friday or Tuesday-Saturday\n     \n     - 8am - 4pm\n     \n     - 9am - 5pm\n     \n     - 10am - 6pm","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$1.5K per month","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"30dcc247-ef2e-4d46-83e4-5eafe6161f3b","tierSummary":"$1.5K per month","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"d97ed58d-b4f2-41be-95a0-66e5883b7750","summary":"$1.5K per month","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 MONTH","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":1500,"maxValue":1500}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 MONTH","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":1500,"maxValue":1500}]}},{"id":"22a94673-4605-4e0e-8979-3b81a59f4e67","title":"Operations Associate (Test Kit)","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City Metro (Remote)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T20:29:02.390+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/22a94673-4605-4e0e-8979-3b81a59f4e67","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/22a94673-4605-4e0e-8979-3b81a59f4e67/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><h1><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You:</strong> An operations-minded problem solver who enjoys owning complex workflows, running customer launches, coordinating across customers and partners, tracking performance, and making sure at-home testing programs run smoothly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Us:</strong> The team responsible for making every test kit experience reliable - from customer launch through fulfillment, laboratory processing, and ongoing operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary:</strong> $80,000 - $95,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location:</strong> NYC metro (remote)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Why we need you</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our Test Kit Operations team ensures that Junction's at-home testing programs launch successfully and operate reliably at scale. Over the past year, test kit volume on our platform has grown 6x, and every program requires coordination across customers, laboratories, fulfillment partners, and internal teams to ensure test kits are delivered, samples are processed, and customers have a seamless testing experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Junction grows, we’re launching more testing programs, supporting more customers, and expanding our network of operational partners. We’re looking for a Test Kit Operations Associate who can take ownership of the operational execution behind these programs.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Once a sale closes, you'll own the launch execution and implementation for every new customer. You're essential in setting our test kit customers up for long-term success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is ideal for someone who enjoys owning complex workflows, bringing structure to moving pieces, and solving operational problems in a fast-growing healthcare environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the operational execution of new customer test kit launches, ensuring milestones are tracked, dependencies are managed, and programs are ready for successful go-live</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate directly with customers to manage launch activities, follow up on open items, and ensure operational requirements are completed on time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with laboratory providers, fulfillment partners, and internal teams to coordinate workflows and keep launches moving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own post-launch monitoring of test kit programs, tracking operational performance and identifying opportunities or issues early</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor key metrics across inventory availability, fulfillment accuracy, shipping timelines, sample processing, turnaround times, and customer experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate operational issues, identify root causes, and work with laboratory and 3PL partners to drive resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain operational dashboards, trackers, and reporting to provide visibility into program health and performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring issues and help implement process improvements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build strong working relationships with customers, laboratory partners, and fulfillment providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document workflows, processes, and best practices</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operations experience:</strong> 3+ years in operations, healthcare operations, logistics, supply chain, customer operations, implementation, or similar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Ownership mindset:</strong> drives things to the finish line without needing constant direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Launch and project execution:</strong> coordinating launches, implementations, or operational programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Problem solving:</strong> digs into root causes and coordinates the right people to resolve</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-functional communication:</strong> comfortable with customers, labs, fulfillment, and internal teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data-driven mindset:</strong> comfortable with spreadsheets, dashboards, and metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Process improvement:</strong> has improved workflows, documentation, or systems before</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Healthcare interest:</strong> healthcare/diagnostics/lab ops/at-home testing experience a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>Nice to have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with labs, diagnostics, or healthcare operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting at-home testing or medical device programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with 3PL providers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing customer implementations or launches</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Looker, Tableau, or similar</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What success looks like</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Launches happen smoothly because you own the details, milestones, and follow-through</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Post-launch programs stay healthy because you monitor, flag risk, and drive resolution</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Customers, labs, and fulfillment partners trust you as a reliable operational owner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Metrics are visible and actionable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recurring issues decrease because you build better process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction can support more programs because of the foundation you help create</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\nSHORT ON TIME? TL;DR\n\nYou: An operations-minded problem solver who enjoys owning complex workflows, running customer launches, coordinating across customers and partners, tracking performance, and making sure at-home testing programs run smoothly.\n\nUs: The team responsible for making every test kit experience reliable - from customer launch through fulfillment, laboratory processing, and ongoing operations.\n\nSalary: $80,000 - $95,000\n\nLocation: NYC metro (remote)\n\n\n\n\nWHY WE NEED YOU\n\nOur Test Kit Operations team ensures that Junction's at-home testing programs launch successfully and operate reliably at scale. Over the past year, test kit volume on our platform has grown 6x, and every program requires coordination across customers, laboratories, fulfillment partners, and internal teams to ensure test kits are delivered, samples are processed, and customers have a seamless testing experience.\n\nAs Junction grows, we’re launching more testing programs, supporting more customers, and expanding our network of operational partners. We’re looking for a Test Kit Operations Associate who can take ownership of the operational execution behind these programs.\n\nOnce a sale closes, you'll own the launch execution and implementation for every new customer. You're essential in setting our test kit customers up for long-term success.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who enjoys owning complex workflows, bringing structure to moving pieces, and solving operational problems in a fast-growing healthcare environment.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING\n\n - Own the operational execution of new customer test kit launches, ensuring milestones are tracked, dependencies are managed, and programs are ready for successful go-live\n\n - Coordinate directly with customers to manage launch activities, follow up on open items, and ensure operational requirements are completed on time\n\n - Partner with laboratory providers, fulfillment partners, and internal teams to coordinate workflows and keep launches moving\n\n - Own post-launch monitoring of test kit programs, tracking operational performance and identifying opportunities or issues early\n\n - Monitor key metrics across inventory availability, fulfillment accuracy, shipping timelines, sample processing, turnaround times, and customer experience\n\n - Investigate operational issues, identify root causes, and work with laboratory and 3PL partners to drive resolution\n\n - Maintain operational dashboards, trackers, and reporting to provide visibility into program health and performance\n\n - Identify recurring issues and help implement process improvements\n\n - Build strong working relationships with customers, laboratory partners, and fulfillment providers\n\n - Document workflows, processes, and best practices\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - Operations experience: 3+ years in operations, healthcare operations, logistics, supply chain, customer operations, implementation, or similar\n\n - Ownership mindset: drives things to the finish line without needing constant direction\n\n - Launch and project execution: coordinating launches, implementations, or operational programs\n\n - Problem solving: digs into root causes and coordinates the right people to resolve\n\n - Cross-functional communication: comfortable with customers, labs, fulfillment, and internal teams\n\n - Data-driven mindset: comfortable with spreadsheets, dashboards, and metrics\n\n - Process improvement: has improved workflows, documentation, or systems before\n\n - Healthcare interest: healthcare/diagnostics/lab ops/at-home testing experience a plus\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with labs, diagnostics, or healthcare operations\n\n - Experience supporting at-home testing or medical device programs\n\n - Experience with 3PL providers\n\n - Experience managing customer implementations or launches\n\n - Familiarity with Looker, Tableau, or similar\n\n\n\n\nWHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE\n\n - Launches happen smoothly because you own the details, milestones, and follow-through\n\n - Post-launch programs stay healthy because you monitor, flag risk, and drive resolution\n\n - Customers, labs, and fulfillment partners trust you as a reliable operational owner\n\n - Metrics are visible and actionable\n\n - Recurring issues decrease because you build better process\n\n - Junction can support more programs because of the foundation you help create\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$80K – $95K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$80K - $95K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bdbdad07-ec18-46c5-9f34-32eed726d67c","tierSummary":"$80K – $95K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"910f9e47-5e36-4b5d-8a07-e9a00c013f3e","summary":"$80K – $95K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":95000},{"id":"df0860b2-d478-48e7-b62b-848ac4e48a1f","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":80000,"maxValue":95000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"5b1234ff-2e9b-485d-97f1-7cd0fb41a2f8","title":"Operations Lead","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"EDT / EST (US East Coast only)","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-24T18:18:08.971+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/5b1234ff-2e9b-485d-97f1-7cd0fb41a2f8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/junction/5b1234ff-2e9b-485d-97f1-7cd0fb41a2f8/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Junction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Backed by <strong>Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC</strong>, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.<br /></p><h2><strong>Short on time? TL;DR</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You: An experienced startup operations leader who enjoys running teams that solve real operational problems every day. You're comfortable managing people, improving processes, and stepping into complex issues when things go wrong.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Us: A growing Lab Operations team responsible for keeping every lab order moving smoothly from order to result. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Salary: $125,000 - $175,000</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Location: Fully remote (US-based, EST timezone required)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Why we need you</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Every lab order that moves through Junction eventually becomes something physical. A kit ships, a lab runs a test, and results make their way back to providers and patients. Lab Operations is the team that makes sure that process works reliably. When they do their job well, customers barely notice. When something goes wrong, they're usually the team that fixes it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As order volume continues to grow, we need someone who can lead the day-to-day operation, coach the team, and make sure quality keeps pace with scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is equal parts people leadership and operational ownership. You'll manage a distributed team, help people make better decisions independently, and improve the systems and processes that support the work. A lot of today's operation is still manual, so there are genuine opportunities to simplify workflows and remove recurring problems over time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll also work closely with Product, Engineering, Customer Success, and our Support teams whenever operational issues need a cross-functional solution or a longer-term fix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing day to day</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage, coach, and develop a distributed Lab Operations team, supporting both individual contributors and team leadership as the organization grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Plan team capacity and staffing as order volume increases based on demand trends</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the team's day-to-day operation across lab result review, order investigations, and proactive issue resolution with labs and customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make sure SLAs, quality standards, and productivity targets are consistently met</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interface with vendors and ensure we have good working relationships, troubleshoot issues as they come up, and set up streamlined processes for day-to-day interaction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Step into complex operational issues when the team needs support, coordinating with Product, Engineering, Customer Success, and external lab partners where needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve SOPs, quality standards, and team workflows so the operation becomes more consistent and easier to scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify recurring operational issues and partner with our Operations Systems &amp; Tooling team on workflow improvements and automation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a team that can solve problems independently, with clear ownership and fewer escalations over time</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>How we measure success</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">SLA attainment across Lab Operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational quality and accuracy as order volume grows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fewer escalations requiring support from senior leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team engagement, development, and retention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Operational improvements that reduce manual work and recurring issues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>People leadership:</strong> 5+ years hiring and managing operations teams through growth. You've coached people to become more independent, handled performance conversations, and built a team that doesn't rely on you for every decision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational judgment:</strong> You've led teams that spend their day solving exception-heavy operational problems rather than simply following scripts. You're comfortable making decisions when situations don't fit neatly into a process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Process improvement:</strong> You've built or significantly improved SOPs, SLAs, quality frameworks, or operational processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Distributed team management:</strong> You've managed people across multiple time zones and know how to build a team rhythm that keeps everyone aligned without constant oversight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Customer and vendor management:</strong> You've handled direct vendor relationships in business-critical operations and are comfortable being the escalation point for customers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Healthcare or operational experience:</strong> You've worked in healthcare operations, diagnostics, logistics, or another operational environment where accuracy matters.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>You don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup experience (Seed -&gt; Series C) highly preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing distributed operations teams based in the Philippines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in lab operations, diagnostics, or healthcare logistics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience partnering with an internal systems or tooling team to automate operational workflows</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company and team offsites</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 monthly wellness budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coworking budget</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Premium healthcare coverage </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% monthly contribution to pension/401k</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Yearly blood test on us</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Important details before applying:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\">more information here</a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"Healthcare is in crisis and the people behind the results deserve better. With more and more data coming from wearables, lab tests, and patient–doctor interactions, we’re entering an era where data is abundant.\n\nJunction is building the infrastructure layer for diagnostic healthcare, making patient data accessible, actionable, and automated across labs and devices. Our mission is simple but ambitious: use health data to unlock unprecedented insight into human health and disease.\n\nIf you're passionate about how technology can supercharge healthcare, you’ll fit right in.\n\nBacked by Creandum, Point Nine, 20VC, YC, and leading angels, we’re working to solve one of the biggest challenges of our time: making healthcare personalized, proactive, and affordable. We’re already connecting millions and scaling fast.\n\n\n\nSHORT ON TIME? TL;DR\n\nYou: An experienced startup operations leader who enjoys running teams that solve real operational problems every day. You're comfortable managing people, improving processes, and stepping into complex issues when things go wrong.\n\nUs: A growing Lab Operations team responsible for keeping every lab order moving smoothly from order to result. \n\nSalary: $125,000 - $175,000\n\nLocation: Fully remote (US-based, EST timezone required)\n\n\n\n\nWHY WE NEED YOU\n\nEvery lab order that moves through Junction eventually becomes something physical. A kit ships, a lab runs a test, and results make their way back to providers and patients. Lab Operations is the team that makes sure that process works reliably. When they do their job well, customers barely notice. When something goes wrong, they're usually the team that fixes it.\n\nAs order volume continues to grow, we need someone who can lead the day-to-day operation, coach the team, and make sure quality keeps pace with scale.\n\nThis role is equal parts people leadership and operational ownership. You'll manage a distributed team, help people make better decisions independently, and improve the systems and processes that support the work. A lot of today's operation is still manual, so there are genuine opportunities to simplify workflows and remove recurring problems over time.\n\nYou'll also work closely with Product, Engineering, Customer Success, and our Support teams whenever operational issues need a cross-functional solution or a longer-term fix.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL BE DOING DAY TO DAY\n\n - Manage, coach, and develop a distributed Lab Operations team, supporting both individual contributors and team leadership as the organization grows\n\n - Plan team capacity and staffing as order volume increases based on demand trends\n\n - Own the team's day-to-day operation across lab result review, order investigations, and proactive issue resolution with labs and customers\n\n - Make sure SLAs, quality standards, and productivity targets are consistently met\n\n - Interface with vendors and ensure we have good working relationships, troubleshoot issues as they come up, and set up streamlined processes for day-to-day interaction\n\n - Step into complex operational issues when the team needs support, coordinating with Product, Engineering, Customer Success, and external lab partners where needed\n\n - Improve SOPs, quality standards, and team workflows so the operation becomes more consistent and easier to scale\n\n - Identify recurring operational issues and partner with our Operations Systems & Tooling team on workflow improvements and automation\n\n - Build a team that can solve problems independently, with clear ownership and fewer escalations over time\n\n\n\n\nHOW WE MEASURE SUCCESS\n\n - SLA attainment across Lab Operations\n\n - Operational quality and accuracy as order volume grows\n\n - Fewer escalations requiring support from senior leadership\n\n - Team engagement, development, and retention\n\n - Operational improvements that reduce manual work and recurring issues\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - People leadership: 5+ years hiring and managing operations teams through growth. You've coached people to become more independent, handled performance conversations, and built a team that doesn't rely on you for every decision.\n\n - Operational judgment: You've led teams that spend their day solving exception-heavy operational problems rather than simply following scripts. You're comfortable making decisions when situations don't fit neatly into a process.\n\n - Process improvement: You've built or significantly improved SOPs, SLAs, quality frameworks, or operational processes.\n\n - Distributed team management: You've managed people across multiple time zones and know how to build a team rhythm that keeps everyone aligned without constant oversight.\n\n - Customer and vendor management: You've handled direct vendor relationships in business-critical operations and are comfortable being the escalation point for customers.\n\n - Healthcare or operational experience: You've worked in healthcare operations, diagnostics, logistics, or another operational environment where accuracy matters.\n\nYou don’t need to tick every box to fit in here. If the problems we’re solving genuinely interest you and you know you can contribute, we’d love to talk.\n\n\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Startup experience (Seed -> Series C) highly preferred\n\n - Experience managing distributed operations teams based in the Philippines\n\n - Experience in lab operations, diagnostics, or healthcare logistics\n\n - Experience partnering with an internal systems or tooling team to automate operational workflows\n\n - Your salary is dependent on your location and experience level\n\n - Equity (extended exercise post 2 years of employment) \n\n - Company and team offsites\n\n - Monthly learning budget of $150 for personal development and productivity\n\n - $100 monthly wellness budget\n\n - Flexible, remote-first working - including $1K for home office equipment\n\n - Coworking budget\n\n - 36 days paid time off (including bank holidays)\n\n - Premium healthcare coverage \n\n - 4% monthly contribution to pension/401k\n\n - Yearly blood test on us\n\n - Enhanced parental, foster, and adoption leave\n   \n   \n\nImportant details before applying:\n\n - We only hire folks physically based in GMT and EST timezones - more information here https://pages.junction.com/Where-we-hire-and-why-218d9955818e802ca48fd1702948e2e3\n\n - We do not sponsor visas right now given our stage","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$125K – $175K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$125K - $175K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"6314144c-e259-4c13-9a6d-f1de09cbf956","tierSummary":"$125K – $175K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"93c37cb5-ddc0-4939-870b-0dbee19a3fb3","summary":"$125K – $175K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":175000},{"id":"8a820da3-4e99-4d28-a429-56048eadf4eb","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":125000,"maxValue":175000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}